WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.088
team for artificial

00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:02.889
intelligence, Jeffrey Hinton

00:00:03.022 --> 00:00:05.091
said he resigned to speak more

00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:06.693
freely about the technology,

00:00:06.826 --> 00:00:09.229
saying it's quickly becoming

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:10.930
smarter than humans.

00:00:11.064 --> 00:00:14.134
You left your job at Google

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:14.868
because you want to focus solely

00:00:15.001 --> 00:00:16.803
on your concerns about ai.

00:00:16.936 --> 00:00:18.405
You've said it could ma nip late

00:00:18.538 --> 00:00:20.373
or possibly figure out a way to

00:00:20.507 --> 00:00:21.541
kill humans?

00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:28.915
How could it kill humans?

00:00:29.048 --> 00:00:30.950
&gt;&gt; If it gets to be much

00:00:31.084 --> 00:00:32.819
smarter, it will gain

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:33.520
manipulation because it will

00:00:33.653 --> 00:00:38.892
have learned that from us.

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:42.128
So it would be a more

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:42.896
intelligent thing being

00:00:43.029 --> 00:00:45.598
controlled by a less intelligent

00:00:45.732 --> 00:00:46.132
thing.

00:00:46.132 --> 00:00:48.334
It can figure out ways of

00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:50.136
manipulating people to do what

00:00:50.136 --> 00:00:50.937
it wants.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.972
&gt;&gt; What do we need to do, pull

00:00:53.106 --> 00:00:55.141
the plug, put in far more

00:00:55.275 --> 00:00:56.676
restrictions and back stops on

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:56.976
this?

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.712
How do we solve this problem?

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:02.282
&gt;&gt; It's not clear to me that we

00:01:02.415 --> 00:01:04.584
can solve this problem.

00:01:04.717 --> 00:01:05.552
I believe we should put a big

00:01:05.685 --> 00:01:07.387
effort into thinking about ways

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.189
to solve the problem.

00:01:09.322 --> 00:01:10.156
I don't have a solution

00:01:10.156 --> 00:01:10.390
presently.

00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:12.158
I just want people to be aware

00:01:12.158 --> 00:01:15.662
that this is a really serious

00:01:15.795 --> 00:01:17.564
problem and we need to be

00:01:17.697 --> 00:01:18.731
thinking about it very hard.

00:01:18.865 --> 00:01:19.766
I don't think we can stop the

00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:20.266
progress.

00:01:20.266 --> 00:01:21.668
I didn't stein the petition

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.169
saying we should stop working on

00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:25.538
ai because if people stopped in

00:01:25.672 --> 00:01:27.340
mesh, people in China wouldn't.

00:01:27.474 --> 00:01:30.176
It's very hard to verify if

00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:30.677
people have been doing it.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.245
&gt;&gt; There have been

00:01:32.378 --> 00:01:34.180
whistle-blowers warning about

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.682
the dangers of ai.

00:01:35.815 --> 00:01:37.717
One was forced out of Google for

00:01:37.851 --> 00:01:38.551
voicing his concerns.

00:01:38.685 --> 00:01:40.820
Looking back, do you wish you

00:01:40.954 --> 00:01:42.555
had stood behind these whistle

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:44.491
blowers more?

00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:46.526
&gt;&gt; That's actually a woman.

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:48.194
&gt;&gt; Oh, sorry.

00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:52.198
&gt;&gt; So they were rather different

00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:52.532
concerns from mine.

00:01:52.665 --> 00:01:54.334
I think it's easier to voice

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.604
concerns if you leave the

00:01:57.737 --> 00:02:04.310
company first.

00:02:04.444 --> 00:02:07.113
D idea is they'll get more

00:02:07.247 --> 00:02:08.748
intelligent and take us over.

00:02:08.882 --> 00:02:10.683
&gt;&gt; Steve Wozniak, to co-founder

00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:12.218
of apple, is also speaking out

00:02:12.318 --> 00:02:15.121
about the dangers of ai.

00:02:15.255 --> 00:02:16.923
&gt;&gt; Ai is another more powerful

00:02:17.056 --> 00:02:18.525
tool and it will be used by

00:02:18.658 --> 00:02:20.460
those people, you know, for

00:02:20.593 --> 00:02:22.228
basically really evil purposes.

00:02:22.228 --> 00:02:23.863
And I hate to see technology

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:24.864
being used that way.

00:02:24.998 --> 00:02:27.534
It shouldn't be, and some --

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:28.234
probably some types of

00:02:28.268 --> 00:02:30.637
regulation are needed.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.240
&gt;&gt; It sounds like you agree.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.341
&gt;&gt; I agree with that, yes.

00:02:35.475 --> 00:02:37.710
&gt;&gt; What should that regulation

00:02:37.844 --> 00:02:40.980
look like?

00:02:41.114 --> 00:02:43.883
&gt;&gt; I'm not often expert on how

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:44.784
to do regulation.

00:02:44.918 --> 00:02:46.419
I'm just a scientist who

00:02:46.553 --> 00:02:47.654
suddenly realized these things

00:02:47.787 --> 00:02:48.988
are getting smarter than us.

00:02:49.122 --> 00:02:51.824
I want to blow the whistle and

00:02:52.258 --> 00:02:52.525
say we should worry seriously

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:54.561
about how we stop these things

00:02:54.694 --> 00:02:56.296
getting control over us.

00:02:56.429 --> 00:02:57.330
And it's going to be very hard.

00:02:57.463 --> 00:02:58.298
And I don't have the solutions.

00:02:58.431 --> 00:02:59.299
I wish I did.

00:02:59.432 --> 00:03:01.568
&gt;&gt; Does there need to be a

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:02.969
meeting of all of the tech

00:03:03.102 --> 00:03:05.038
groups and governments working

00:03:05.171 --> 00:03:07.640
on this, Google, China,

00:03:07.774 --> 00:03:10.276
whatever, in some sort of set of

00:03:10.276 --> 00:03:11.611
rules of the road?

00:03:11.744 --> 00:03:13.179
How do we've pardon text against

00:03:13.313 --> 00:03:16.749
bad actors or rogue nations

00:03:16.883 --> 00:03:19.953
harnessing ai?

00:03:20.286 --> 00:03:22.455
&gt;&gt; So, for some things it's very

00:03:22.589 --> 00:03:28.294
hard like using ai for

00:03:28.394 --> 00:03:29.062
manipulating electrics or for

00:03:29.195 --> 00:03:30.797
soldiers but for the existential

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.298
threats taking over, we're all

00:03:32.398 --> 00:03:33.232
in the same boat.

00:03:33.366 --> 00:03:34.968
It's bad for all of us.

00:03:35.101 --> 00:03:36.402
So we might be able to get China

00:03:36.536 --> 00:03:38.304
and the U.S. To agree on things

00:03:38.304 --> 00:03:38.838
like that.

00:03:38.972 --> 00:03:40.306
It's like nuclear weapons.

00:03:40.373 --> 00:03:42.308
If there's a nuclear war, we all

00:03:42.308 --> 00:03:44.811
lose, and it's the same if these

00:03:44.944 --> 00:03:45.311
things take over.

00:03:45.445 --> 00:03:47.080
So since we're all in the same

00:03:47.213 --> 00:03:48.748
boat, we should be able to get

00:03:48.881 --> 00:03:49.482
agreement between China and the

00:03:49.616 --> 00:03:50.850
U.S. On things like that.

00:03:50.984 --> 00:03:51.784
&gt;&gt; Do you think tech companies

00:03:51.918 --> 00:03:54.320
will be the solution or are they

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.324
so invested in this financially

00:03:58.424 --> 00:03:59.826
and also, let's be frank, in

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:02.462
terms of power, that they're not

00:04:02.595 --> 00:04:07.400
going to be part of the solution

00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:07.700
here?

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.268
&gt;&gt; I think the tech companies

00:04:09.402 --> 00:04:10.603
are the people most likely to be

00:04:10.737 --> 00:04:10.780
able to see how to keep this

